      resolucion: "The Investigating Court issued dismissal order 404/2025 after evaluating the new expert evidence. The court considered that there was no evidence of tax fraud and that the irregularities were accounting errors. The dismissal was confirmed by the Provincial Court. Our client was exonerated and the Tax Agency continued the administrative procedure separately.",
      marco_legal: "The case was framed in article 305 of the Criminal Code on tax fraud. The court applied the requirement that tax fraud requires intention to defraud and falsification of documents. The judgment emphasized that mere accounting irregularities are not sufficient for criminal conviction. The case established an important precedent on the distinction between accounting errors and tax fraud."
